From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: siraisisatoru <37771374+siraisisatoru@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:58:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] umac_connection: derive a zero passphrase_len from the
 passphrase

struct mmwlan_sta_args documents that passphrase_len "may be zero if
passphrase is null-terminated", and umac_connection_validate_sta_args()
checks the passphrase that way. umac_connection_start(), however, sets
the stored length from the SSID:

    data->sta_args.passphrase_len = strlen((const char *)data->sta_args.ssid);

The stored length is then used when the supplicant config is built
(config_populate_network_security() copies exactly passphrase_len
bytes into sae_password), so with MMWLAN_SAE and passphrase_len == 0:

  - if the SSID is shorter than the passphrase, the SAE password is
    silently truncated and authentication fails against a correctly
    configured AP;
  - if the SSID is longer, the copy includes the terminating NUL and
    whatever follows it in the passphrase buffer;
  - a 32 byte SSID has no terminator in mmwlan_sta_args.ssid, so the
    strlen() itself reads beyond the array.

In relay mode the effect also reaches the downstream BSS:
umac_relay_start_relay_ap() copies sta_args.passphrase_len into the
repeater's mmwlan_ap_args, so the repeater AP is brought up with the
same wrong SAE password.

Compute the length from the passphrase, bounded by
MMWLAN_PASSPHRASE_MAXLEN as in umac_connection_validate_sta_args().
---
 framework/morselib/src/umac/connection/umac_connection.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/framework/morselib/src/umac/connection/umac_connection.c b/framework/morselib/src/umac/connection/umac_connection.c
index a26fb9cc..62784405 100644
--- a/framework/morselib/src/umac/connection/umac_connection.c
+++ b/framework/morselib/src/umac/connection/umac_connection.c
@@ -362,7 +362,8 @@ enum mmwlan_status umac_connection_start(struct umac_data *umacd,
     }
     else
     {
-        data->sta_args.passphrase_len = strlen((const char *)data->sta_args.ssid);
+        data->sta_args.passphrase_len =
+            strnlen(data->sta_args.passphrase, MMWLAN_PASSPHRASE_MAXLEN);
     }
 
     if (args->extra_assoc_ies_len != 0 && extra_assoc_ies != NULL)
